window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>They bound me to her with blood.<br>Long before I even knew what love was.</p><p>I was ten when the ritual united us.<br>A sacred vow.<br>A whispered command.<br>Protect her—no matter the cost.</p><p>But no one asked me if I could survive losing her.</p><p>Now she is gone—my vow buried with her.<br>And in her place stands the girl who carries her blood.<br>The one I was never meant to want.<br>The one they hunted through fire, through silence, across marble floors drenched in blood.</p><p>Elaria Fontanesi steps broken into my world.<br>A daughter of betrayal.<br>A girl forged in grief.<br>She doesn’t know who I am.<br>Or what I did to protect the house that destroyed hers.<br>But fate has no patience.<br>And the past does not stay buried.<br>We are bound again—by legacy, by duty, by a lie sealed in shadow.</p><p>She sees the scars I never let anyone see.<br>And I feel the pull I swore I would never answer again.<br>This isn’t devotion.<br>It’s obsession, veiled in loyalty.<br>A love that should have died with her sister…<br>But refuses to stay in the grave.</p><p>I was her protector.<br>Now I could be her ruin.<br>And God help me—perhaps I would let it happen.</p>"; 
